MUSIC MACRO LANGUAGE (MML)
==========================

MML source files define music tracks for the SSG and FM channels of the YM2610.
Tracks are compiled by sound/tools/mml_compile.py into Z80 data tables
(sound/driver/music_data.inc) that the driver's Timer B engine executes.
The music engine can layer SSG notes with inline ADPCM-A, ADPCM-B, and FM
triggers inside a single looping track.

MML SOURCE FILES
----------------
  0_samurai_game_loop.mml   — In-game SSG loop (playMusic(0))
  1_samurai_battle_loop.mml — Battle scene SSG loop (playMusic(1))
  2_samurai_night_scene.mml — Night scene SSG loop (playMusic(2))

Track numbers come from alphabetical sort of filenames.
Adding or renaming files changes the track number mapping.

COMMAND REFERENCE
-----------------
  A-G [n]    : Note with optional length suffix (e.g. C4 = quarter, C8 = eighth)
  + or #     : Sharp modifier after note letter
  -          : Flat modifier after note letter
  R [n]      : Rest for duration n
  O n        : Set octave (0-7)
  < / >      : Decrease / increase octave by one
  L n        : Set default note length (4=quarter, 8=eighth, 16=sixteenth, etc.)
  T n        : Set tempo
  V n        : Set SSG volume (0-15)
  ~          : Loop back to start of track
  @aN        : Trigger ADPCM-A sample N inline
  @bN        : Trigger ADPCM-B sample N inline
  @fN        : Trigger FM track N inline (N = 0..FM_TRACK_COUNT-1)

LAYERING NOTES
--------------
  Use one `playMusic(n)` call as the owner of the musical scene.
  Put long ADPCM-B beds and FM counter-lines inline in that music track.
  Avoid starting standalone SSG tracks from inside normal music flow; the main
  music engine already owns the SSG side.

BUILDING
--------
  make mml               : compile all .mml files
  make sound / sound-all : full sound rebuild including MML
